  profile's line_xyz.xml: a composite frame of the type NETEX_LIGNE holding a
  general frame NETEX_LIGNE_STRUCTURE — the line, its route, stop points
  assigned to the quays of stop.xml, its journey pattern — and a general frame
  NETEX_HORAIRE with three journeys, one on each day type of resource.xml.
  Their passing times name no point of the pattern: NeTEx 1.x leaves the
  reference out (PassingTimeGroup, netex_passingTimes_version.xsd), and the
  French deliveries write the times in the order of the pattern's points.
  NeTEx 2.0 requires the reference and an identifier of the passing time:
  this document is valid for the release the profile is written for, 1.x.
  Written for netex-rs's tests (MIT OR Apache-2.0); places, lines and times
  are invented.
-->
